      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سوّق</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسْوِيقٌ</span>: see 1, first sentence. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سوّق فُلَانًا أَمْرَهُ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>He made such a one to have the
ruling,</i> or <i>ordering, of his affair,</i> or <i>case.</i> (Ibn-
'Abbád, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also 5. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Said of a plant,
(TA,) or of a tree, (K,) more properly of the
former, (TA,) (assumed tropical:)  <i>It had a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاق</span> [i. e. <i>stem, stock,</i>
or <i>trunk</i>]. (K, TA.)

